.TH S3M 7 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m \- parallel S3 object manager: conventions shared by all tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
s3m is a set of command line tools that parallelise traditionally
single-threaded object storage operations against Amazon S3 and
S3-compatible services (MinIO, Ceph RGW, Wasabi, Backblaze B2,
Cloudflare R2, and others).
They shard the key space by prefix, keep many requests in flight across
a pool of worker threads, and batch mutations.
.SS Tools
.TP
.BR s3m\-ls (1)
Parallel bucket lister.
.TP
.BR s3m\-du (1)
Parallel usage reporter.
.TP
.BR s3m\-rm (1)
Parallel remover.
.TP
.BR s3m\-ver (1)
Version and delete-marker manager.
.TP
.BR s3m\-sync (1)
Parallel synchroniser.
.TP
.BR s3m\-cp (1)
Parallel copy.
.TP
.BR s3m\-find (1)
Parallel find.
.TP
.BR s3m\-diff (1)
Parallel comparison.
.SH CONVENTIONS
.IP \(bu 2
Targets are
.B s3://BUCKET
(the whole bucket) or
.B s3://BUCKET/PREFIX
(every key starting with PREFIX).
.IP \(bu 2
Output is CSV with a header row and RFC 4180 quoting.
Row order is non-deterministic because the work is parallel.
.IP \(bu 2
Anything that changes the object store is a
.B dry run by default.
.B \-\-apply
is the only way to change anything; there is deliberately no
.B \-\-dry\-run
flag.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads
sets the worker pool size (default 16, maximum 256).
S3 concurrency is latency-bound rather than CPU-bound, so raise it
freely for large jobs.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-o " FILE"
writes the output to FILE and shows a live progress block on the
terminal;
.B \-q
silences stdout only.
.IP \(bu 2
Errors are per entry: counted, the first 24 collected, and reported on
stderr at the end.
A run never aborts part-way because of one failing entry.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
prints the suite version; every tool reports the same number.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
Every tool accepts the same connection options.
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " URL"
S3 endpoint, for example
.BR https://minio.example.com:9000 .
Default: AWS,
.BR https://s3.REGION.amazonaws.com .
.TP
.BI \-\-region " R"
SigV4 signing region.
Non-AWS services usually accept any value.
Default
.BR us\-east\-1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Profile to read from
.I ~/.aws/credentials
and
.IR ~/.aws/config .
.TP
.B \-\-path\-style
Use path-style addressing
.RB ( host/bucket/key )
instead of virtual-hosted
.RB ( bucket.host/key ).
Enabled automatically when the endpoint host is an IP address,
.BR localhost ,
or a single-label name.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sign
Anonymous (unsigned) access, for public buckets.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-bundle " FILE"
CA bundle for endpoints with a private CA.
.SH RESOLUTION ORDER
Flags win, then environment, then profile files, then defaults.
.TP
Endpoint
.B \-\-endpoint
\(->
.B S3M_ENDPOINT
\(->
.B AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3
\(->
.B AWS_ENDPOINT_URL
\(-> profile
.B endpoint_url
\(-> AWS regional endpoint.
.TP
Region
.B \-\-region
\(->
.B AWS_REGION
\(->
.B AWS_DEFAULT_REGION
\(-> profile
.B region
\(->
.BR us\-east\-1 .
.TP
Profile
.B \-\-profile
\(->
.B AWS_PROFILE
\(->
.BR default .
.TP
Credentials
.B AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
and
.B AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
(plus
.BR AWS_SESSION_TOKEN )
\(-> profile in
.I ~/.aws/credentials
\(-> profile in
.IR ~/.aws/config .
.PP
If no credentials are found the tool refuses to start; pass
.B \-\-no\-sign
explicitly for anonymous access.
Requests are signed with AWS Signature Version 4.
.SH LOAD BALANCING ACROSS ENDPOINT ADDRESSES
The tools that run a worker pool against S3 accept
.BR \-\-rrdns .
It resolves the endpoint hostname (A and AAAA records) once at startup
and gives each worker thread its own address from the list, round
robin.
With more threads than addresses, several threads share an address.
.PP
The TCP connection is pinned to the thread's address, but the
.B Host
header, TLS SNI and the SigV4 signature keep the original hostname, so
certificates and Host-validating gateways are unaffected.
If a thread's address fails (connection errors, timeouts, or 429/408/5xx
after the retry budget is spent) the thread moves to the next address
in the list.
The endpoint must be a hostname, not a literal IP address.
.SH RETRIES
Throttling responses (HTTP 429, 503
.BR SlowDown )
and transient transport errors are retried up to 8 times with
exponential backoff and jitter.
Uploads use
.B UNSIGNED\-PAYLOAD
streaming; use HTTPS endpoints if payload signing matters to your
threat model.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.aws/credentials
.TQ
.I ~/.aws/config
Profiles.
.B AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE
and
.B AWS_CONFIG_FILE
relocate them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Completed with errors.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, startup failure, or a safety-guard refusal.
.PP
.BR s3m\-diff (1)
uses diff-like codes instead; see its page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m\-ls (1),
.BR s3m\-du (1),
.BR s3m\-rm (1),
.BR s3m\-ver (1),
.BR s3m\-sync (1),
.BR s3m\-cp (1),
.BR s3m\-find (1),
.BR s3m\-diff (1)
.PP
